{% set local_problem %}
<p>Somerville's rural character means heavy tree coverage on most properties. Pine needles are a constant problem — they slip through large-opening guards and accumulate year-round. Hardwood leaves add to the burden in fall, and the combination keeps gutters filling constantly.</p>

<p>For many Somerville homeowners, gutter cleaning becomes an exhausting chore. Rural properties with multiple outbuildings might have hundreds of feet of gutters to clean. Climbing ladders multiple times a year is time-consuming, inconvenient, and risky.</p>

<p>The bigger concern is what happens between cleanings. When gutters clog during heavy storms, water overflows toward your foundation. On clay soil, that overflow pools and persists.</p>

<p>Gutter guards solve this permanently. Install once, and the cleaning burden is essentially eliminated.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers that fit over or inside your gutters, allowing water through while blocking debris. Different types work better for different challenges.</p>

<p>Micro-mesh guards with tiny perforations excel at blocking fine debris like pine needles. For Somerville's pine-heavy properties, this is usually the best choice.</p>
{% endset %}

